1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,877
有个问题，听起来很简单
Here's a question that sounds easy.

2
00:00:02,197 --> 00:00:05,722
井字棋有多少种不同的对局？这里说的“一局”
How many different games of tic-tac-toe are there? By a game,

3
00:00:05,722 --> 00:00:08,500
指的是从第一步到最后一步、按顺序排好的全部走法
we mean the whole list of moves, in order.

4
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,683
所以，如果两局最后的棋盘一样
So if two games end with the same board,

5
00:00:10,683 --> 00:00:14,896
但走棋的顺序不同，那它们要算作两种不同的对局
but the moves happened in a different order, they count as two different games.

6
00:00:15,216 --> 00:00:17,861
棋盘翻转或旋转后得到的对局，也分开算
Flipped or turned versions count separately too.

7
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,473
猜一猜
Take a guess.

8
00:00:20,523 --> 00:00:22,613
一百？一百万？
A hundred? A million?

9
00:00:22,933 --> 00:00:25,195
暂停一下视频，把你猜的数写下来
Pause the video and write your guess down.

10
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:37,572
答案是 255,168
The answer is 255,168.

11
00:00:37,892 --> 00:00:41,361
在这个视频里，我们会弄清楚这个数字是怎么来的
In this video we'll find out where that number comes from:

12
00:00:41,361 --> 00:00:47,044
先仔细地算，再用一段短短的电脑程序，把每一局都下一遍
first by careful counting, and then with a short computer program that plays every single game.

13
00:00:48,083 --> 00:00:50,024
先看一个更简单的问题
Let's start with a simpler question.

14
00:00:50,344 --> 00:00:55,720
假设有人三子连成一线了，双方也不停，一直下到九个格子都填满
Suppose the players ignore three in a row, and just keep going until all nine squares are full.

15
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:58,686
填满棋盘有多少种不同的顺序？
In how many different orders can the board fill up?

16
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:01,813
X 先走，有 9 个格子可以选
X goes first and has 9 squares to choose from.

17
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:04,864
不管 X 下在哪儿，O 都还剩 8 个格子
For each of those, O has 8 squares left.

18
00:01:05,184 --> 00:01:08,586
这就是 9 个 8，所以选择数要相乘
That's 9 groups of 8, so the choices multiply:

19
00:01:08,586 --> 00:01:12,949
9 乘 8 等于 72，前两步就有 72 种不同的下法
9 times 8 is 72 different ways to make the first two moves.

20
00:01:13,183 --> 00:01:18,132
继续乘下去：9 乘 8 乘 7，依此类推，一直乘到 1
Keep going: 9 times 8 times 7, and so on, all the way down to 1.

21
00:01:18,452 --> 00:01:21,186
数学家给这种连乘起了个名字
Mathematicians have a short name for this:

22
00:01:21,186 --> 00:01:24,831
9 的阶乘，写成 9 后面加一个感叹号
nine factorial, written as a 9 with an exclamation mark.

23
00:01:25,151 --> 00:01:28,735
它等于 362,880
It equals 362,880.

24
00:01:28,983 --> 00:01:34,146
可是，等一下。这比 255,168 还要多
But wait. That's more than 255,168.

25
00:01:34,466 --> 00:01:36,066
我们算出来的太多了
Our count is too high.

26
00:01:36,236 --> 00:01:38,476
这些多出来的对局，都是从哪儿来的？
Where are all those extra games coming from?

27
00:01:40,117 --> 00:01:41,454
问题就在这儿
Here's the catch.

28
00:01:41,504 --> 00:01:45,109
真正的井字棋，一有人三子连成一线，就结束了
Real tic-tac-toe stops as soon as someone gets three in a row.

29
00:01:45,429 --> 00:01:50,101
这一局，X 在第 5 步就赢了，所以剩下的四个格子从没下过
In this game, X wins on the fifth move, so the last four squares are never played.

30
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:54,806
可是 362,880 还是把这几步没下的棋也算进去了
But our 362,880 counted those missing moves anyway,

31
00:01:54,806 --> 00:01:58,563
就好像赢了以后，双方还在接着下
as if the players kept going after the win.

32
00:01:58,883 --> 00:02:03,101
填满这 4 个空格子，有 4 乘 3 乘 2 乘 1
The 4 empty squares can be filled in 4 times 3 times 2 times 1,

33
00:02:03,101 --> 00:02:04,701
也就是 24 种不同的顺序
so 24 ways.

34
00:02:04,921 --> 00:02:07,609
所以这一局被算了 24 次！
So this one game got counted 24 times!

35
00:02:07,929 --> 00:02:10,467
我们把这些编出来的对局叫作“幽灵对局”
Let's call those made-up endings ghost games.

36
00:02:10,787 --> 00:02:13,369
我们要让每一局真实的对局都只算一次
We want to count each real game only once.

37
00:02:13,617 --> 00:02:15,217
一局最早什么时候能结束？
So when can a game end?

38
00:02:15,366 --> 00:02:16,966
至少要到第 5 步
Not before move 5.

39
00:02:17,073 --> 00:02:18,804
X 下的是第 1、3、5 步
X plays moves 1, 3 and 5,

40
00:02:18,804 --> 00:02:23,238
所以到了第 5 步，才可能有人凑齐三个棋子
so the fifth move is the first time anyone can have three marks.

41
00:02:23,484 --> 00:02:27,409
暂停想一想：有多少种对局是 X 在第 5 步赢下的？
Pause and ponder: how many games end with X winning on move 5?

42
00:02:27,729 --> 00:02:29,670
先自己算一算，再看答案
Try to count them before I show you.

43
00:02:49,917 --> 00:02:51,752
这里有个办法，分三个步骤
Here's one way, in three steps.

44
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:54,205
第一，选出 X 获胜的那条线
First, pick the line X wins with.

45
00:02:54,525 --> 00:02:58,173
一共有 8 条：3 排、3 列和 2 条对角线
There are 8: 3 rows, 3 columns and 2 diagonals.

46
00:02:58,493 --> 00:03:01,557
第二，X 可以按不同的顺序填满这条线
Second, X fills that line in some order:

47
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:05,618
3 乘 2 乘 1，也就是 3 的阶乘，所以有 6 种顺序
3 times 2 times 1, which is 3 factorial, so 6 orders.

48
00:03:05,938 --> 00:03:10,312
第三，第一个 O 有另外 6 个格子可以选
Third, O's first mark can go on any of the other 6 squares,

49
00:03:10,312 --> 00:03:14,984
第二个 O 还剩 5 个格子可以选：6 乘 5 等于 30 种放法
and O's second mark on any of the 5 left: 6 times 5 is 30 ways.

50
00:03:15,304 --> 00:03:20,573
把它们乘起来：8 乘 6 乘 30 等于 1,440 种对局
Multiply: 8 times 6 times 30 is 1,440 games.

51
00:03:22,417 --> 00:03:24,721
那 O 在第 6 步赢下的对局呢？
What about games that O wins on move 6?

52
00:03:25,041 --> 00:03:26,641
O 需要三子连成一线
O needs three in a row.

53
00:03:26,854 --> 00:03:30,222
但要小心：如果三个 X 也连成了一线
But careful: if X's three marks also make a line,

54
00:03:30,222 --> 00:03:34,897
X 在第 5 步就已经赢了，还没等 O 连完，这一局就结束了
X already won on move 5, and the game stopped before O could finish.

55
00:03:35,134 --> 00:03:38,194
还是用那三个步骤：O 有 8 条线可选
Use the same three steps: 8 lines for O,

56
00:03:38,194 --> 00:03:44,009
O 填满这条线有 6 种顺序，三个 X 有 6 乘 5 乘 4 种放法
6 orders for O's marks, and 6 times 5 times 4 ways to place X's three marks.

57
00:03:44,329 --> 00:03:48,382
这样，O 一共有 5,760 种方法连成一线
That's 5,760 ways for O to finish a line.

58
00:03:48,702 --> 00:03:53,590
然后再减去 432 种情况：三个 X 也连成了一线
Then we subtract the 432 where X's three marks made a line too,

59
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:58,323
正好是和 O 那条线平行的一排或一列，所以 X 抢先赢了
a row or column parallel to O's, so X sneaked in a win first.

60
00:03:58,643 --> 00:04:01,523
最后剩下 5,328 种对局
That leaves 5,328 games.

61
00:04:01,767 --> 00:04:05,796
在第 7、8、9 步结束的对局就麻烦多了
For games that end on moves 7, 8 and 9, it gets much worse:

62
00:04:05,796 --> 00:04:09,074
我们必须检查之前的每一步有没有人赢
we'd have to check every earlier move for a win,

63
00:04:09,074 --> 00:04:11,943
而且下满的棋盘可能是有人赢，也可能是平局
and a full board might be a win or a draw.

64
00:04:12,263 --> 00:04:14,055
这就变成了一团乱麻
It turns into a tangled mess.

65
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,180
手算变得这么乱的时候，我们还有 Plan B
When counting gets this messy, there's another plan.

66
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,100
别再想巧办法了
Don't count cleverly.

67
00:04:19,164 --> 00:04:21,431
不如教电脑学会规则
Instead, teach a computer the rules,

68
00:04:21,431 --> 00:04:24,455
再让它一局接一局，把所有可能的对局都下一遍
and let it play every possible game, one by one.

69
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,505
首先，电脑需要一个棋盘
First, the computer needs a board.

70
00:04:27,825 --> 00:04:29,511
我们用一个列表来存 9 个格子
We'll use a list of 9 squares.

71
00:04:29,831 --> 00:04:32,774
我们用的编程语言叫 Python
In Python, the programming language we're using,

72
00:04:32,774 --> 00:04:35,962
在 Python 里，列表里的位置从零开始编号
the spots in a list are numbered starting from zero,

73
00:04:35,962 --> 00:04:38,108
所以格子的编号是 0 到 8
so our squares are numbered 0 to 8.

74
00:04:38,428 --> 00:04:40,199
空格子里放一个点
An empty square holds a dot.

75
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:44,489
接下来，电脑要知道怎样才算赢
Next, the computer needs to know what counts as a win.

76
00:04:44,809 --> 00:04:46,918
我们直接把所有能赢的线都列出来
We simply list all 8 winning lines,

77
00:04:46,918 --> 00:04:48,990
一共 8 条，每条线写成一组三个格子编号
as groups of three square numbers.

78
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:51,892
0、1、2 号格组成最上面一排
Squares 0, 1 and 2 make the top row.

79
00:04:52,212 --> 00:04:54,985
0、4、8 号格组成一条对角线
Squares 0, 4 and 8 make a diagonal.

80
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,807
接下来是一个函数：在编程里，函数就是一小段有名字的程序
Next comes a function: a little mini-program with a name.

81
00:05:00,127 --> 00:05:03,010
这个函数叫 winner，意思是“赢家”，它会检查每一条线
This one, called winner, checks every line.

82
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:07,117
如果一条线上三个格子放的都一样，而且不是点
If all three squares on a line hold the same mark, and that mark isn't a dot,

83
00:05:07,117 --> 00:05:08,717
那这是谁的棋子，谁就赢了
that player has won.

84
00:05:08,937 --> 00:05:10,299
如果没有一条线符合
If no line matches,

85
00:05:10,299 --> 00:05:14,036
winner 什么也没找到，就返回 None，意思是“没有人”
winner finds nothing, and hands back None, which means nobody.

86
00:05:14,983 --> 00:05:16,088
最巧妙的部分来了
Now for the clever part:

87
00:05:16,088 --> 00:05:18,804
一个叫 explore 的函数，explore 就是“探索”的意思
a function called explore.

88
00:05:18,854 --> 00:05:20,306
我们告诉它轮到谁
We tell it whose turn it is,

89
00:05:20,306 --> 00:05:24,455
它的任务是统计从现在这个棋盘往后，还可能出现多少局
and its job is to count every game that can still happen from the current board.

90
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,599
它一开头就是两个停止条件
It starts with two stopping rules.

91
00:05:26,919 --> 00:05:29,951
如果已经有人赢了，那就是下完的一局
If someone has already won, that's one finished game,

92
00:05:29,951 --> 00:05:31,953
所以 explore 返回数字 1
so explore hands back the number 1.

93
00:05:32,273 --> 00:05:36,668
如果棋盘满了却没有人赢，那就是平局，也算下完的一局
If the board is full with no winner, that's a draw, also one finished game.

94
00:05:36,916 --> 00:05:39,028
否则，这一局就还没结束
Otherwise, the game isn't over yet.

95
00:05:39,348 --> 00:05:41,524
于是 explore 会试每一个空格子
So explore tries every empty square.

96
00:05:41,844 --> 00:05:45,948
它在那里放上这一方的棋子，再问自己同一个问题
It puts the player's mark there, and then asks itself the same question,

97
00:05:45,948 --> 00:05:49,481
这次轮到对方：从这里往后，还能下出多少局？
now for the other player: how many games can happen from here?

98
00:05:49,801 --> 00:05:51,444
它把所有的答案加起来
It adds up all the answers.

99
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:54,751
我们把第一个小棋盘放大看看，这时轮到 O
Let's zoom into the first of those, with O to move.

100
00:05:55,071 --> 00:05:58,506
如果 O 下在右上角那格，O 就赢了：算 1 局
If O takes the top-right square, O wins: that's 1 game.

101
00:05:58,826 --> 00:06:01,578
擦掉它，这回试试上边中间那格
Erase it, and try the top-middle square instead.

102
00:06:01,898 --> 00:06:05,162
然后 X 填上最后一格，结果是平局：再算 1 局
Then X fills the last square, and it's a draw: 1 more.

103
00:06:05,482 --> 00:06:08,191
撤销这两步，再加起来：2 局
Undo both moves, and add up: 2 games.

104
00:06:08,511 --> 00:06:12,180
再算上另外两个分支，2 加 1 加 2 等于 5
With the other two branches, 2 plus 1 plus 2 makes 5.

105
00:06:12,416 --> 00:06:14,187
像这样，函数自己调用自己
When a function calls itself,

106
00:06:14,187 --> 00:06:18,155
也就是自己问自己同一个问题，就叫作递归
asking itself the same question like this, it's called recursive.

107
00:06:18,475 --> 00:06:20,948
听起来好像会没完没了
That might sound like it goes on forever,

108
00:06:20,948 --> 00:06:25,109
但每调用一次就多一个棋子，所以总会碰到停止条件
but each call adds one more mark, so a stopping rule always kicks in.

109
00:06:25,429 --> 00:06:27,136
想象一棵倒过来的树
Picture an upside-down tree.

110
00:06:27,456 --> 00:06:31,308
空棋盘在最上面，每一种可能的走法是一个分支
The empty board is at the top, every possible move is a branch,

111
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:33,387
而下完的每一局都是一片叶子
and every finished game is a leaf.

112
00:06:33,707 --> 00:06:35,813
我们的 explore 会沿着每一条分支往下走
Explore walks down every branch,

113
00:06:35,813 --> 00:06:38,507
一次走一条，再数一数走到了多少片叶子
one at a time, and counts the leaves it reaches.

114
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:41,182
还有一行代码，很容易被忽略
There's one more line, and it's easy to miss.

115
00:06:41,502 --> 00:06:45,769
程序下每一局都用同一个棋盘，就像只有一块白板
The program plays every game on just one board, like a single whiteboard.

116
00:06:46,089 --> 00:06:49,161
所以每探索完一步，它就要擦掉那个棋子
So after exploring a move, it erases that mark.

117
00:06:49,481 --> 00:06:53,406
这叫“撤销”这一步，这样棋盘恢复原样，下一个分支就能接着试
That's called undoing the move, and it means the next branch starts fresh.

118
00:06:53,726 --> 00:06:58,120
先试走一条路，再退回来试下一条，这就叫回溯
Trying a path, then stepping back to try the next one, is called backtracking.

119
00:07:00,267 --> 00:07:03,936
想弄懂一个程序，有个好办法：故意把它改坏
A great way to understand a program is to break it on purpose.

120
00:07:04,256 --> 00:07:08,416
暂停想一想：如果删掉“撤销”那一行，你觉得会发生什么？
Pause and ponder: what do you think happens if we delete the undo line?

121
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:20,293
程序只输出 3
The program prints just 3.

122
00:07:20,613 --> 00:07:23,002
没有了撤销，什么都不会被擦掉
Without undo, nothing ever gets erased.

123
00:07:23,322 --> 00:07:27,102
程序先下一局，按顺序一格一格地填
The program plays one game, filling the squares in order,

124
00:07:27,102 --> 00:07:29,423
直到 X 在第 7 步连成一条对角线
until X makes a diagonal on move 7.

125
00:07:29,743 --> 00:07:34,629
这是第 1 局。接着它去试 X 的其他下法，可是原来那个 X 还在
That's 1. Then it tries X's other choices, but the old X is still there.

126
00:07:34,949 --> 00:07:40,730
X 下在下边中间那格，原来那条对角线又算赢了一次：这是第 2 局
X lands on the bottom-middle square, and the old diagonal counts as a win again: that's 2.

127
00:07:41,050 --> 00:07:43,247
然后是右下角那格：第 3 局
Then the bottom-right square: that's 3.

128
00:07:43,567 --> 00:07:46,554
现在棋盘满了，再也没有可以试的了
Now the board is full, so there's nothing left to try.

129
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,102
现在把“撤销”那一行放回去，改成删掉“判断输赢”
Now put undo back, and delete the winner check instead,

130
00:07:50,102 --> 00:07:52,624
这样对局要等棋盘满了才会停
so games only stop when the board is full.

131
00:07:52,944 --> 00:07:54,630
暂停一下，先猜猜答案
Pause and predict the answer.

132
00:08:04,867 --> 00:08:07,768
362,880
362,880.

133
00:08:08,088 --> 00:08:09,688
这正是 9 的阶乘！
That's nine factorial!

134
00:08:09,838 --> 00:08:13,385
没有了判断输赢，程序在有人赢了之后还会接着下
Without the winner check, the program keeps playing after a win,

135
00:08:13,385 --> 00:08:15,214
所以它把所有幽灵对局都算进去了
so it counts all the ghost games.

136
00:08:15,534 --> 00:08:17,667
它自己又找回了我们最早算出的那个数
It rediscovered our very first count.

137
00:08:18,717 --> 00:08:21,917
现在，我们把每一行都放回去，运行真正的程序
Now let's put every line back and run the real program.

138
00:08:22,237 --> 00:08:26,760
过了一小会儿，它输出了 255,168
After a moment, it prints 255,168.

139
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,624
我们按对局在第几步结束，把这个总数拆开来看
Let's split that total by when each game ends.

140
00:08:29,944 --> 00:08:32,287
1,440 局在第 5 步结束
1,440 end on move 5,

141
00:08:32,287 --> 00:08:38,733
5,328 局在第 6 步结束，和我们手算的结果一样
and 5,328 on move 6, the same numbers we found by hand.

142
00:08:39,053 --> 00:08:40,854
然后柱子一下子升高了
Then the bars shoot up:

143
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:45,475
约 4.8 万局在第 7 步结束，7.3 万局在第 8 步结束
about 48 thousand end on move 7, and 73 thousand on move 8.

144
00:08:45,795 --> 00:08:49,624
有一半多一点的对局会下满 9 步
Just over half of all games use all 9 moves:

145
00:08:49,624 --> 00:08:53,453
约 8.2 万局是 X 赢，还有 46,080 局是平局
about 82 thousand X wins, plus 46,080 draws.

146
00:08:53,773 --> 00:08:57,806
加起来就是 255,168
Together, that's 255,168.

147
00:08:58,050 --> 00:09:00,461
再来看看，这和 9 的阶乘有什么关系
And here's how it connects to nine factorial.

148
00:09:00,781 --> 00:09:05,374
还记得吗，9 的阶乘把在第 5 步结束的每一局
Remember, nine factorial counted each game that ends on move 5

149
00:09:05,374 --> 00:09:08,930
都算了 24 次，每个幽灵对局算一次
a total of 24 times, once for each ghost ending.

150
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:14,114
在第 6 步结束的一局被算了 6 次，在第 7 步结束的，算了两次
A game ending on move 6 was counted 6 times, and on move 7, twice.

151
00:09:14,434 --> 00:09:16,188
在第 8 步或第 9 步结束的对局
Games that end on move 8 or 9

152
00:09:16,188 --> 00:09:19,938
最多只剩一个空格子，所以它们只算了一次
have at most one empty square, so they were counted just once.

153
00:09:20,258 --> 00:09:22,401
把每根柱子乘上各自被算的次数
Multiply each bar by its number,

154
00:09:22,401 --> 00:09:26,018
再全部加起来，正好又是 9 的阶乘
add them up, and you get exactly nine factorial again.

155
00:09:28,334 --> 00:09:29,934
谁赢的对局最多？
Who wins the most games?

156
00:09:30,169 --> 00:09:40,345
X 赢了 131,184 局，O 赢了 77,904 局，还有 46,080 局是平局
X wins 131,184 of them, O wins 77,904, and 46,080 are draws.

157
00:09:40,665 --> 00:09:43,683
在所有可能的对局里，X 赢的超过一半
X wins in more than half of all possible games,

158
00:09:43,683 --> 00:09:46,766
因为先走让 X 有更多机会赢
because going first gives X more chances to win.

159
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,465
最后一道题
One last puzzle.

160
00:09:48,515 --> 00:09:52,014
X 的第一步下在哪儿，能下出的不同对局最多
Which first move for X leads to the most different games:

161
00:09:52,014 --> 00:09:54,040
角上、边上，还是中心？
a corner, an edge, or the center?

162
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,960
暂停一下，猜一猜
Pause and guess.

163
00:10:05,684 --> 00:10:08,350
没想到吧：答案是边格，也就是每条边正中间的那一格
Surprise: the edge,

164
00:10:08,350 --> 00:10:10,356
有 29,592 种对局
with 29,592 games.

165
00:10:10,676 --> 00:10:19,721
每个角格有 27,732，而中心最少，只有 25,872。为什么？
Each corner gives 27,732, and the center the fewest, just 25,872. Why?

166
00:10:20,041 --> 00:10:24,927
中心在 4 条获胜线上，角格在 3 条上，而边格只在 2 条上
The center sits on 4 winning lines, a corner on 3, and an edge on just 2.

167
00:10:25,247 --> 00:10:29,311
线越多，X 越有机会在第 5 步或第 7 步提前赢
More lines give X more chances to win early, on move 5 or 7,

168
00:10:29,311 --> 00:10:32,969
而每一次提前赢，都会从树上砍掉一大片分支
and every early win chops whole branches off the tree.

169
00:10:33,217 --> 00:10:35,948
但要小心：能下出的对局多，不代表这一步更好
But careful: more games doesn't mean a better move.

170
00:10:36,268 --> 00:10:40,534
在所有先下中心的对局里，X 每 10 局大约赢 6 局
Out of all the games that start in the center, X wins about 6 in 10.

171
00:10:40,854 --> 00:10:43,521
先下边格的话，X 赢不到一半
Starting on an edge, X wins fewer than half.

172
00:10:45,567 --> 00:10:47,978
那么，先走的 X 是不是总能赢？
So does going first mean X always wins?

173
00:10:48,298 --> 00:10:51,071
不是。电脑能做的，不只是统计对局
No. A computer can do more than count.

174
00:10:51,391 --> 00:10:55,807
它从树的最底下开始，那里每一局都已经下完，然后一层一层往上推
It starts at the bottom of the tree, where every game is finished, and works upward.

175
00:10:56,127 --> 00:10:58,767
每到一个分支，它都挑最好的一步
At every branch it picks the best move:

176
00:10:58,767 --> 00:11:02,356
轮到 X 时挑对 X 最好的，轮到 O 时挑对 O 最好的
best for X on X's turns, and best for O on O's turns.

177
00:11:02,676 --> 00:11:05,142
这样一来，它就把井字棋彻底算透了
Doing that, it has solved tic-tac-toe:

178
00:11:05,142 --> 00:11:08,906
如果双方都不失误，每一局都会是平局
if both players play perfectly, every game ends in a draw.

179
00:11:09,226 --> 00:11:12,959
所以 X 赢下的每一局，都少不了 O 在某一步的失误
So every one of X's wins needs a mistake by O somewhere.

180
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,021
国际象棋也能这样算吗？
Could we do the same for chess?

181
00:11:17,341 --> 00:11:18,635
完全不可能
Not a chance.

182
00:11:18,685 --> 00:11:23,561
1950 年，数学家兼工程师克劳德·香农估计
In 1950, the mathematician and engineer Claude Shannon estimated

183
00:11:23,561 --> 00:11:28,285
国际象棋至少有 10 的 120 次方种可能的对局
that chess has at least 10 to the power of 120 possible games.

184
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:31,357
那可是 1 后面跟着 120 个零！
That's a 1 followed by 120 zeros!

185
00:11:31,677 --> 00:11:36,584
而我们能观测到的整个宇宙，也只有大约 10 的 80 次方个原子
The whole observable universe has only about 10 to the power of 80 atoms.

186
00:11:36,834 --> 00:11:39,501
所以，国际象棋程序没法探索每一个分支
So chess programs can't explore every branch.

187
00:11:39,821 --> 00:11:43,587
它们只往后看几步，再估计谁更有希望赢
They look only so many moves ahead, then estimate who's winning,

188
00:11:43,587 --> 00:11:46,882
靠的是从几百万局练习中学到的经验
using what they learned from millions of practice games.

189
00:11:47,202 --> 00:11:50,473
但说到底，思路和你刚学的一样
But underneath, it's the same idea you just learned:

190
00:11:50,473 --> 00:11:53,431
把走法排成一棵树，一个分支一个分支地探索
a tree of moves, explored one branch at a time.

191
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:55,240
我们来小结一下
Let's recap.

192
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:57,825
把每一步的选择数乘起来
Multiplying the choices

193
00:11:57,825 --> 00:12:01,903
就得到 9 的阶乘，一共 362,880 种顺序
gives nine factorial, 362,880 orders.

194
00:12:02,223 --> 00:12:06,426
但只要有人赢，对局就会停下，所以这些顺序里有很多都是幽灵对局
But games stop when someone wins, so many of those orders are ghost games.

195
00:12:06,746 --> 00:12:08,647
而一段短短的递归程序
And a short recursive program

196
00:12:08,647 --> 00:12:13,039
先试走一步，往下探索，再撤销，就把每一局真实对局都统计了一遍
counts every real game by trying a move, exploring, and undoing it.

197
00:12:13,359 --> 00:12:18,095
答案正好是 255,168
The answer is exactly 255,168.

198
00:12:18,334 --> 00:12:19,799
现在，轮到你了
Now it's your turn.

199
00:12:19,849 --> 00:12:23,548
改一改程序，让它只统计 X 赢的对局
Change the program so it counts only the games X wins,

200
00:12:23,548 --> 00:12:28,617
或者只统计在第 7 步结束的对局，或者看看如果 O 先走会怎样
or only the games that end on move 7, or see what happens if O goes first.

201
00:12:28,937 --> 00:12:32,393
程序和挑战题的链接都在视频简介里
The program and the challenges are linked in the description.

202
00:12:32,713 --> 00:12:34,313
动手去探索吧！
Have fun exploring!
